  {"i":2858,"t":["communication","city"],"s":{},"n":"住所 is personal information written on forms and letters and names a place in town. It is not about the house or its rooms."},
  {"i":2860,"t":["school","travel"],"s":{"3":["sports"],"5":["food"],"6":["food"]},"n":"Course of study is the core sense, and a route or trail is a hiking or sightseeing course. Travel in t already covers sense 1, so it needs no separate entry."},
  {"i":2894,"t":["food"],"s":{"2":["feelings"],"3":["feelings"]},"n":"Bitter is taught with the other taste words in the food unit, so qualities adds nothing. The figurative senses go to feelings."},
  {"i":2904,"t":["actions"],"s":{},"n":"Putting something into operation is a general action. The link to law is too loose for a learner-level unit."},
  {"i":2968,"t":["actions","home"],"s":{"2":["technology"]},"n":"洗濯物を取り込む is the typical everyday use and belongs with housework. Capturing or importing data is technology."},
  {"i":2990,"t":["routine","family"],"s":{"4":["food"]},"n":"Putting a child to bed is routine and family. 生地を寝かせる (letting dough rest) is a common cooking sense, so sense 4 goes to food."}
