 "d": [
  {"i":2860,"keep":[3,5],"n":"Swimming and running lanes (第3コース) and meal courses (コース料理) are common senses with their own units. Sense 6 repeats the food sense of 5."},
  {"i":2874,"keep":[],"n":"'Tune, melody' is a literary sense, rare for learners."},
  {"i":2878,"keep":[2],"n":"'Suited to' (子供向き) is a common N3 sense and has nothing to do with position."},
  {"i":2885,"keep":[],"n":"'Being at odds' is a figurative extension. The core sense is movement."},
  {"i":2889,"keep":[1],"n":"Breaking a bone (骨を折る) is a common sense, taught with injuries in the health unit."},
  {"i":2894,"keep":[],"n":"A bitter look and a bitter experience are figurative uses of the taste word."},
  {"i":2903,"keep":[],"n":"'Quality' is rare as しな. 品がいい uses the reading ひん."},
  {"i":2907,"keep":[],"n":"'Mala fides' is a technical legal sense, rare at this level."},
  {"i":2909,"keep":[4],"n":"Iced drinks (アイスコーヒー) are common and belong in drink. Plain ice is 氷, so アイス for ice is rare."},
  {"i":2923,"keep":[],"n":"Controlling emotions with this word is less common for learners. The machine sense fits 't'."},
  {"i":2930,"keep":[],"n":"The card suit is a rare sense for learners."},
  {"i":2951,"keep":[],"n":"Bare グラス for eyewear is rare. Learners meet it as サングラス or 眼鏡."},
  {"i":2952,"keep":[],"n":"The counting device and the counter-attack senses are rare for learners. Service and bar counters fit 't'."},
  {"i":2953,"keep":[2],"n":"Feeling embarrassed when praised is a common everyday sense and belongs with emotions."},
  {"i":2959,"keep":[2],"n":"Headhunting staff is a common sense and is taught in the work unit."},
  {"i":2963,"keep":[2],"n":"Going against a law or rule (法律に反する) is common and belongs in law."},
  {"i":2964,"keep":[4],"n":"Entering data is a common sense in technology. 'Devote oneself' is not specifically about hobbies."},
  {"i":2968,"keep":[2],"n":"Importing or capturing data and images is a common sense in technology."},
  {"i":2975,"keep":[2],"n":"'Talkative person' is a common sense, taught as a personality trait."},
  {"i":2980,"keep":[2],"n":"'Two degrees' is common for temperature and fits the units of measurement."},
  {"i":2982,"keep":[3],"n":"Calling a young man (お)兄さん is common everyday usage, taught in the people unit."},
  {"i":2990,"keep":[4],"n":"Letting dough rest or letting food age is a common cooking sense."},
  {"i":2995,"keep":[3],"n":"One point in an exam or a match is common and is taught in both school and sports."}
